@prefix : <#> .
@prefix schema: <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<> a schema:CreativeWork ;
    schema:name "Full Skills Contract Always Applies — Regardless of Request Phrasing"@en ;
    schema:description "Softer request phrasing ('RDF and HTML collection', 'thesis and value prop analysis') does not license a lighter cut of the kg-generator/rdf-infographic-skill contract. FAQ, Glossary, HowTo, and resolver-wrapped entity hyperlinks are mandatory regardless of whether the user says 'infographic'."@en ;
    schema:dateCreated "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema:dateModified "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema:author <https://linkedin.com/in/kidehen#this> ;
    schema:about :fullSkillsContractGate ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <../preferences.ttl#step-fullSkillsContractAlwaysApplies>,
        <../preferences.ttl#step-structuralContractDetails>,
        <../preferences.ttl#step-countReflectsSourceDensity>,
        <faq-entity-iri-gate.ttl>, <entity-href-companion-ttl.ttl>,
        <rdf-infographic-compliance-gate.ttl> .

:fullSkillsContractGate a schema:HowTo ;
    schema:name "Full Skills Contract Gate"@en ;
    schema:description "Blocking checklist run before delivering any RDF+HTML(+MD) collection, regardless of how the user phrased the request."@en ;
    schema:step :step-faqMinimum, :step-glossaryMinimum, :step-howtoWhenProcedural,
        :step-countReflectsSourceDensity,
        :step-bodyProseResolverLinks, :step-verifyBeforeDelivery,
        :step-faqIsAccordion, :step-glossaryIsIndexNotAccordion, :step-navInactivityFadeRequired .

:step-faqMinimum a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    schema:name "FAQ section: at least 10 schema:Question entities, covering every distinct question-worthy claim in the source"@en ;
    schema:text "Each schema:Question carries schema:name, schema:acceptedAnswer, and schema:parentItem back to the schema:FAQPage. Fewer than 10 is a contract violation, caught 2026-07-22 when only 5 were delivered for a 'collection' request that wasn't labeled 'infographic' — but 10 is the floor, not the target; see step-countReflectsSourceDensity for the completeness requirement above that floor."@en .

:step-glossaryMinimum a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    schema:name "Glossary: at least 10 schema:DefinedTerm entities, covering every distinct term the source introduces or defines"@en ;
    schema:text "Each schema:DefinedTerm carries schema:name, schema:description, and schema:inDefinedTermSet back to the schema:DefinedTermSet. Fewer than 10 is a contract violation, caught 2026-07-22 when only 6 were delivered — but 10 is the floor, not the target; see step-countReflectsSourceDensity for the completeness requirement above that floor."@en .

:step-howtoWhenProcedural a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 3 ;
    schema:name "Add a schema:HowTo section whenever the source material contains procedural content"@en ;
    schema:text "If the analyzed source(s) contain any setup, quick-start, configuration, or step-by-step procedure (e.g. a README 'Quick start' section), model it as a schema:HowTo with ordered schema:HowToStep entities — do not omit it just because the user's request didn't use the word 'howto'. Caught 2026-07-22: a repository quick-start section existed in the source material but no HowTo section was produced. HowTo has no numeric floor at all — it is the model step-countReflectsSourceDensity generalizes to FAQ and glossary: content-gated, not count-gated."@en .

:step-countReflectsSourceDensity a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 4 ;
    schema:name "10 is an anti-under-delivery floor for FAQ and glossary, never a ceiling — the delivered count must track the source's actual content density"@en ;
    schema:text """Added 2026-08-01, prompted by a review of the fixed '>= 10' FAQ/glossary rule against NeurOWL-style completeness thinking (arXiv:2607.15776, applied here to knowledge-graph narrative sections rather than ontology axioms): a fixed floor guards against under-delivery but says nothing about over-thin coverage once 10 is reached. This step closes that gap.

Before finalizing FAQ and glossary sections:
(a) Enumerate every distinct question-worthy claim in the source material (a claim is question-worthy if a reader would plausibly ask "why/how/what is this" about it and the source has a distinct answer — not every sentence, but every distinct claim).
(b) Enumerate every distinct term the source introduces, uses as jargon, or explicitly defines.
(c) The delivered FAQ/glossary count must cover both enumerations in full. If the enumeration yields fewer than 10 distinct items, do NOT pad with invented or marginal entries just to hit the floor — flag the shortfall and ask the user whether to proceed under 10 or broaden the source. If the enumeration yields more than 10, deliver all of them — the count is not capped at 10.
(d) This mirrors step-howtoWhenProcedural's already-content-gated approach: HowTo has no numeric floor because its trigger is "does procedural content exist," not "did we hit a number." FAQ and glossary keep the 10-floor as a distinct anti-under-delivery guardrail (validated by real incidents, see step-faqMinimum/step-glossaryMinimum), but above that floor the same content-gated logic applies.

This step does not relax step-faqMinimum or step-glossaryMinimum — it adds a completeness ceiling-removal on top of the existing floor."""@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <../preferences.ttl#step-countReflectsSourceDensity> .

:step-bodyProseResolverLinks a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 5 ;
    schema:name "Resolver-wrap entity mentions in body prose, not just the footer"@en ;
    schema:text "Every entity heading or mention in the article body — thesis-quote attributions, principle/value-proposition/open-question card headings, inline source citations — must be a resolver-wrapped hyperlink (https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url={encoded-entity-IRI}) built from the companion TTL's own entity IRIs (DAV-base + fragment for document-local entities; the direct verified external IRI — DBpedia, homepage, source post — for external entities). Footer/hero-meta tool-attribution credits (kg-generator, rdf-infographic-skill, URIBurner, Virtuoso, the LLM's own homepage) remain the one documented exception and keep plain canonical-homepage links per entity-href-companion-ttl.ttl step 4. Caught 2026-07-22: resolver-wrapping was applied correctly to footer/hero-meta credits but the body prose (thesis blockquote, principle list, value-prop cards, open-question cards, source citations) used plain external hrefs."@en .

:step-verifyBeforeDelivery a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 6 ;
    schema:name "Run the blocking grep checks before calling the deliverable done"@en ;
    schema:text """grep -c 'describe/?url=%23' file.html   # MUST be 0 — bare-fragment hrefs resolve to nothing
grep -oc 'linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=' file.html   # should be a large count spanning every section, not just the footer
python3 -c "import rdflib; g=rdflib.Graph(); g.parse('file.ttl'); from rdflib.namespace import Namespace; s=Namespace('http://schema.org/'); import rdflib as r; print(len(list(g.subjects(r.RDF.type, s.Question))), len(list(g.subjects(r.RDF.type, s.DefinedTerm))))"   # both must be >= 10"""@en .

:step-faqIsAccordion a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 7 ;
    schema:name "FAQ MUST be a real accordion — div[role=button] + max-height panel, never <details>/<summary>"@en ;
    schema:text "rdf-infographic-skill/SKILL.md Core Architecture item 7: 'FAQ Accordion — Common questions with smooth expand/collapse'. The required markup (from faq-entity-iri-gate.ttl step-writeHtmlHref) is a `.faq-item` wrapping a `.faq-q` div with `role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"` containing the resolver-linked question `<a>` (with `onclick=\"event.stopPropagation()\"` so the link doesn't fire the toggle) plus a chevron `.faq-indicator` span, and a sibling `.faq-a > .faq-a-inner` answer panel toggled via a `toggleFaq(el)` JS function adding/removing `.open` on `.faq-item` (CSS: `max-height:0` collapsed, `max-height:400px` when `.open`, with a transition). Do NOT use native `<details>/<summary>` — caught 2026-07-23 after first delivering exactly that anti-pattern. Also do NOT nest `<a>` inside `<button>` — invalid HTML, seen even in an older reference file this corpus otherwise reuses."@en .

:step-glossaryIsIndexNotAccordion a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 8 ;
    schema:name "Glossary is an 'interactive entity index,' NOT an accordion — do not add expand/collapse by false analogy with the FAQ fix"@en ;
    schema:text "rdf-infographic-skill/SKILL.md Core Architecture item 8: 'Glossary/Definitions — Interactive entity index with external links' (contrast with item 7's explicit 'Accordion... expand/collapse' wording for FAQ). 'Interactive' means resolver-linked term names, not a toggle widget. Render as a card grid (`.gloss-grid` > `.gloss-card` with the term name as a resolver-wrapped `<h4><a>` and the definition as plain visible text below) — never collapsed by default. Flagged 2026-07-23 when a user asked 'ditto Glossary' immediately after the FAQ-accordion fix; the correct response was to distinguish the two contract items, not add matching accordion behavior to glossary."@en .

:step-navInactivityFadeRequired a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 9 ;
    schema:name "Floating nav MUST implement a 2-minute inactivity fade with a dynamically created reactivation marker — a second IIFE, separate from drag+collapse"@en ;
    schema:text "rdf-infographic-skill/SKILL.md 'Navigation Control' section: after 2 minutes with no mousemove/keydown/scroll/click/touchstart, the nav fades via opacity:0 + pointer-events:none; a small ☰ reactivation marker (created dynamically in JS, same top/right position as the nav, one z-index above) becomes visible; any activity or clicking the marker resets the 2-minute timer and restores the nav. This is a SEPARATE IIFE from the drag+collapse-toggle IIFE with its own timer/reset logic — building only the drag+collapse IIFE silently omits this required behavior with no visible symptom until a user actually waits two minutes and notices the nav never fades. Caught 2026-07-23: the first-delivered nav JS had drag+collapse+theme-toggle but no fade timer at all. RECURRENCE (2026-08-10): Claude Sonnet 5, kg-generator + rdf-infographic-skill task (Vivian Voss 'The Tool That Was Already There') — first-delivered nav JS had a fade timer, but folded into the SAME function as collapse-toggle (not a separate IIFE), faded only to opacity:.25 (not opacity:0 + pointer-events:none), and created no reactivation marker at all — so the faded nav was still fully interactive and there was no way to bring it back to full opacity except ambient activity. The nav also had no drag or resize capability, a separate SKILL.md Navigation Control requirement ('always-visible compact header, toggle, draggable, resizable') that was skipped entirely, not just weakened. Same session also shipped the glossary as an index-chips + `<dl>` list instead of the required `.gloss-grid > .gloss-card` card grid (see step-glossaryIsIndexNotAccordion). User caught all of this by asking why the delivered HowTo/FAQ page wasn't 'to skills contract or prefs' after the routing/filename issue was raised in the same message. Corrected by splitting into two IIFEs (drag+collapse-toggle vs. a separate navInactivityFade with a dynamically-created #navReactivate marker gated by the same manuallyHidden flag), adding CSS resize:both plus a mousedown/mousemove/mouseup drag handler on the nav header, and switching the glossary markup to .gloss-grid/.gloss-card. Confirms the harness-contract items in this file are not satisfied by 'a fade exists' or 'an interactive index exists' — the exact required mechanics (separate IIFE, opacity:0+pointer-events:none+marker, drag+resize, card-grid class names) must each be checked individually against this document before delivery, not inferred from a functionally-similar but structurally different implementation."@en .
